<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zou Yan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 305–240 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zou Yan was a Chinese philosopher of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a> associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jixia-academy">Jixia Academy</a> in Qi. He is regarded as the founder of the Yin-Yang school, combining the theory of yin and yang with the cycle of the Five Phases, which he used to explain the rise and fall of dynasties. His cosmology strongly influenced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> thought, though his writings are lost.</p></div>
